    "description": "``exec()`` is used to execute a command with the underlying operating system. It is the equivalent of ``shell_exec()`` and back-ticks. \n\n``exec()`` has specific arguments to collect both the result of the command, one line per element in an array, and the resulting code. This differs from ``shell_exec()``, which only returns the result, and as a string.",
